    "recommendations": "Reducing vegetation density immediately surrounding the structure, including brush and other vegetation in direct contact with or adjacent to exterior walls and attachments, could meaningfully improve defensible space and reduce the opportunity for fire to reach the structure. Creating and maintaining separation between shrubs, trees, and ground-level fuels near the structure may reduce fuel continuity across the property. Where continuous grass cover and heavy ground vegetation are present, periodic mowing or removal during dry seasonal periods could reduce surface fuel loads. Managing vegetation along the length of the driveway and access route would support firefighter access and improve evacuation conditions. Maintaining the irrigated landscaping near the structure as a managed, lower-fuel zone could further support a functional defensible space perimeter. Given the limited defensible space observed, prioritizing vegetation management closest to the structure and along the primary access route would provide the most immediate benefit to overall wildfire resilience and suppression support."
